# {{NAME}}

A paper project of the visual-geometry stack, laid out by the stack's
paper-project conventions
([Paper projects](https://visualgeometrytoolkit.github.io/VisualGeometryToolkitEval/stable/paper-projects/)
in the VisualGeometryToolkitEval documentation): a [DrWatson](https://juliadynamics.github.io/DrWatson.jl/)
project whose every result comes from a driver under `scripts/` run on a
config of record under `configs/`, and whose suite enforces the conventions.

```
julia --project=. -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.instantiate()'
julia --project=. scripts/example_stage.jl --plan     # the stage plan
julia --project=. scripts/example_stage.jl            # run what is pending
julia --project=. test/runtests.jl                    # the conventions + the project's tests
```

A driver renders under `plots/` and its `deploy` stage copies the renders into the paper
(`deploy_assets`): a new asset goes in, a changed one only with `--replace-submitted`, the
sign-off. A full reproduction is reviewed before it reaches the paper: with `--results-branch`
the driver skips `deploy` and puts its renders on a branch `results/<UTC stamp>-<commit>` of this repository,
in a worktree of its own (under `VGTK_RESULTS_WORKTREES`, else `<repository>-results` beside
it), with `RUN.toml` (the commit, the run keys, the data tiers, the machine) and `COMPARISON.md`
(every number against the paper as committed on its branch, IMPROVED or DEGRADED by the direction its
`add_number!(…; better)` states). Then, in Julia (`using VisualGeometryToolkitEval.Reproduce`):

```
accept_results(".", "results/<stamp>-<commit>"; replace_submitted = true)   # one merge commit, tag accepted/<stamp>;
                                                                            # this checkout fast-forwards (its post-merge hook runs)
remove_results_worktree(".", "results/<stamp>-<commit>")                    # after acceptance, or as the rejection
remove_results_worktree(".", "results/<stamp>-<commit>"; delete_branch = true)
```

| Path | Holds |
|---|---|
| `configs/` | the configs of record (TOML): every value a result depends on |
| `scripts/` | the drivers: one per paper asset, stage-idempotent (`--plan`, `--stage=NAME`, `--force`) |
| `src/` | the shared prelude (`{{NAME}}.jl`) the drivers include |
| `test/` | the suite; `runtests.jl` calls `paper_project_violations` |
| `{{PAPERDIR}}/` | the paper; generated assets under `{{FIGDIR}}/` |
| `data/exp_raw` | the read-only inputs (a link or directory per machine, or the artifact view; `data/README.md`) |
| `data/exp_pro` | the results, in directories keyed by run key, each with its `_provenance.toml` |
| `plots/` | the drivers' renders (not tracked); the `deploy` stage copies the paper's into `{{FIGDIR}}/` |
| `REPRODUCE.md` | the asset index: every figure, table and macro the paper reads → its generator, config and data |
| `Artifacts.toml`, `configs/data_artifacts.toml` | the published input data (Zenodo) and their catalog |
